From: elkir0 <elkir0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pipeline: simple: Add the Galaxy Tab S2 camera receiver

The Samsung Galaxy Tab S2 (SM-T715) captures raw Bayer frames from its
Exynos 5433 MIPI CSI-2 receivers through FIMC-LITE straight to memory,
with no ISP in between: the t715-camera driver registers one media
device per camera, with the sensor and the capture video node the
simple pipeline handler expects, so frames have to be debayered in
software.

Add "t715-camera" to the list of supported devices with the software
ISP enabled. It is this repository's own kernel driver
(kernel/patches/t715-parity, kernel/patches/t715-camera-af), so it will
not be sent upstream.
---
 src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
index bfadaf9..46af46f 100644
--- a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
@@ -267,6 +267,7 @@ static const SimplePipelineInfo supportedDevices[] = {
 	{ "mxc-isi", {}, false },
 	{ "qcom-camss", {}, true },
 	{ "sun6i-csi", {}, false },
+	{ "t715-camera", {}, true },
 };
 
 bool isRaw(const StreamConfiguration &cfg)
